  "title": "Chapter 11: Metals and Non-metals",
  "order": 60,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fcersym",
      "content": "Metals and non-metals are two major categories of elements found in nature. They differ in their physical and chemical properties. Metals are generally good conductors of heat and electricity, while non-metals usually act as poor conductors. Understanding their properties helps in identifying their uses in industries and daily life."
    },
