    {
      "id": "0cri5o7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Metals and non-metals are distinguished by distinct physical traits like malleability, ductility, and electrical conductivity.",
        "Chemical classification shows metals typically form basic oxides while non-metals form acidic or neutral oxides.",
        "The Reactivity Series ranks metals in decreasing order of their chemical activity.",
        "The methods for extraction of metals depend directly on their position in the reactivity series."
      ],
      "id": "6n537tn"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jll45kl",
      "content": "• Metals are elements that are generally hard, shiny and good conductors of heat and electricity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k754hmf",
      "content": "• They are usually solid at room temperature (except mercury)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3uj3497",
      "content": "• Examples: Iron, Copper, Aluminium, Gold, Silver."
    },
    {
      "id": "vd4rcdr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Physical Properties of Metals"
    },
    {
      "id": "1zs4ol9",
