          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Lustre</p>",
            "<p>Metals have shiny surfaces.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Malleability</p>",
            "<p>Metals can be hammered into thin sheets.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Ductility</p>",
            "<p>Metals can be drawn into wires.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Conductivity</p>",
            "<p>Good conductors of heat and electricity.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>High melting point</p>",
            "<p>Most metals have high melting points.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x5bzdh3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Chemical Properties of Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bmuqe5w",
      "content": "• Metals react with oxygen to form metal oxides."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u2usq4h",
      "content": "• Metals react with water to produce hydrogen gas."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dugw076",
      "content": "• Metals react with acids to produce hydrogen gas."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9o28ynw",
      "content": "• Metals lose electrons to form positive ions."
    },
    {
      "id": "pt1rj3v",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Non-metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hbvv99j",
      "content": "• Non-metals are elements that are generally dull and poor conductors of heat and electricity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xlag2wk",
      "content": "• They may exist in solid, liquid or gaseous state."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vrcx65m",
      "content": "• Examples: Oxygen, Nitrogen, Carbon, Sulfur."
    },
    {
      "id": "y3u8yta",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Physical Properties of Non-metals"
    },
    {
      "id": "qbose7q",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
