      "id": "2wjijzh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Extraction of Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Exceptions in physical properties (e.g., liquid metal Mercury, lustrous non-metal Iodine, soft metals Sodium/Potassium) are highly tested.",
        "Order of elements in the Reactivity Series and displacement reactions frequently appear in multiple-choice questions.",
        "Distinction between roasting (in presence of air) and calcination (in limited air) is a standard topic in metallurgical questions."
      ],
      "id": "tvekuaw"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6c1rie7",
      "content": "• Highly reactive metals are extracted by electrolysis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "25np5p5",
      "content": "• Moderately reactive metals are extracted by reduction using carbon."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "686ubdi",
      "content": "• Less reactive metals are often found in free state."
    },
    {
      "id": "41xl5wv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vetec0y",
      "content": "• Metals are good conductors of heat and electricity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qse6dor",
      "content": "• Non-metals are generally poor conductors."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l23gis3",
      "content": "• Mercury is the only metal that is liquid at room temperature."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wa3tg06",
      "content": "• Gold and silver are least reactive metals."
    }
  ],
